  <body>
    <div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: bold;"><big><big><big>Christine's
              Recipes<br>
              <br>
            </big></big></big></span>
      <div style="text-align: left;"><small>I collected these recipes and put
          them online for a few different purposes.&nbsp; First of all, I travel
          a lot and this way I don't have to bring all of my notebooks and
          cookbooks with me.&nbsp; I also always know where my latest version of
          a recipe is.&nbsp; It makes it easier to share my recipes.&nbsp; I'm
          also trying to teach other grad students how to cook and most of these
          recipes are relatively simple.&nbsp; Another, more devious motivation
          is to hook my non-American friends on American cooking.&nbsp; I'm also
          trying to promote traditional American cooking and show people that
          American cuisine does go beyond hamburgers and french fries.<br>
          <br>
          These are family recipes, recipes I made up myself, recipes I changed
          from their original form, and a few I got out of books when the recipe
          was either perfect or something I make rarely so didn't have notes on
          what I'd done the last time.&nbsp; (As I change recipes, my favorite
          version will be put up here.)&nbsp; I cited sources, except for a few
          I got from my Mom which I didn't have time to add citations to.<br>
          <br>
          This is intended for my family and friends.&nbsp; There are
          typos.&nbsp; I mix unit systems sometimes so Americans may need to
          look at the unit conversion page.<br>
        </small></div>
      <small><span style="font-weight: bold;"></span></small> </div>
    <small><br>
